    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** headlining the roster as our primary catalyst. With a score of 80.13, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is an elite play, buoyed significantly by a plus-matchup against Dobbins and the inherent scarcity of his stolen base profile, which continues to be our highest priority. **Yordan Alvarez** (62.19) and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.18) provide high-floor power production in prime leadoff and two-hole spots, respectively. While **Junior Caminero** (60.55) faces a left-handed starter in Rogers, his xwOBA of 0.373 and premium spot in the third position keep him firmly in the strong-start tier, defying typical platoon concerns.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision centered on **Dillon Dingler**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 37.83 efficiency score. While he benefits from the park factors associated with the Burke matchup, his dynamic platoon disadvantage (-15%) rendered him a liability compared to the collective floor provided by **Colt Keith** (50.09) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (51.76). We are opting to keep **Dillon Dingler** and **Chase Meidroth** on the bench to preserve our game caps, as their sub-40 scores fall below our established threshold for active participation.\n\nManaging risk remains paramount given the schedule volatility. **Gary Sanchez** faces a stern test against Skubal, whose 2.77 xERA suppresses **Gary Sanchez**'s score to a marginal 41.99; he remains active only due to positional scarcity. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor **Trea Turner** and **Christian Yelich**, both of whom are sidelined today. Should these bench pieces remain inactive for an extended duration, we may need to pivot towards depth options like **Josh Smith** or **Casey Schmitt** to maintain our competitive pace in the 5x5 categories.",
